WEBVTT
NOTE SYNC_TYPE: HUMAN_VERIFIED
NOTE Track: 1-11 - Last Bus Home: Lights Out on Progress Street
NOTE Artist: The Stardust Engine
NOTE Album: Progress Street (2004)

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.800
[Instrumental Intro — Grand Piano Chords, Warm Analog Synth Pad & Melodic Guitar Lead]

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:25.200
The final spotlight fades across the empty arena floor

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:33.000
The road cases are latched and rolled outside the stage door

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:40.267
For twenty years we gave the world the thunder in our chest

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:46.169
Now the highway's calling us to finally take our rest

00:00:47.172 --> 00:00:54.500
Our custom low-floor shuttle bus is kneeling at the curb

00:00:54.500 --> 00:01:02.500
Leading to a quiet place the static can't disturb.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:08.500
Aluminum ramp unfolds beneath the amber sign

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:15.500
Five of us together at the end of the line!

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:22.500
We're taking the last bus home! Back to Progress Street!

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:29.500
Turning off the amplifiers and the stadium heat!

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:34.200
Lock the front door tight and let the curtains fall

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:38.800
We don't owe the outside world anything at all!

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:42.301
Through every storm we weathered and every song we played

00:01:42.381 --> 00:01:48.544
This family is the greatest music that we ever made!

00:01:52.806 --> 00:02:00.000
Unplug the synthesizers, set the guitars in their stands

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Rest the tired voices and the callused, aching hands

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:13.940
Five pairs of sneakers lined up by the wooden stairs

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:19.221
Trading all the crowded rooms for quiet living room chairs

00:02:20.481 --> 00:02:27.500
We're not fading into nothing, we're just tuning out the noise

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:34.500
Back to three sisters and brothers and the twin Wright boys!

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:41.500
We're taking the last bus home! Back to Progress Street!

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:48.500
Turning off the amplifiers and the stadium heat!

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:52.819
Lock the front door tight and let the curtains fall

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:56.382
We don't owe the outside world anything at all!

00:02:56.502 --> 00:03:00.500
Through every storm we weathered and every song we played

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:05.710
This family is the greatest music that we ever made!

00:03:18.141 --> 00:03:25.000
Someday when we're ready, we'll turn the switches on

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:32.784
And find out that the fire in the engine's never gone

00:03:33.024 --> 00:03:40.045
But tonight the porch light's turning off in Blacksburg town

00:03:40.105 --> 00:03:47.507
As we lay the heavy burden of the road right down!

00:03:47.507 --> 00:04:13.500
[Guitar Solo — Epic 1980s Stadium-Rock Guitar Solo Over Grand Piano & Analog Synths]

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:20.500
We're taking the last bus home! Back to Progress Street!

00:04:21.309 --> 00:04:28.555
Turning off the amplifiers and the stadium heat!

00:04:28.615 --> 00:04:31.437
Lock the front door tight and let the curtains fall

00:04:31.497 --> 00:04:35.020
We don't owe the outside world anything at all!

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:39.500
Through every storm we weathered and every song we played

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:45.168
This family is the greatest music that we ever made!

00:04:49.872 --> 00:04:53.602
Lights out on Progress Street...

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:57.500
Goodnight, Forger Nation.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:24.500
[Outro — Warm Sustained Piano & Analog Synth Chord Fading into Silence]
